                <pb facs="0553" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.1153 Smith Company, Werner G./77:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-06T17:00:00-05:00">December 6, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>640. Your 1423, November 18, 7 p.m., wood oil. Werner G. Smith authorizes
                    acceptance of Japanese offer to pay for the remaining part of the shipment
                    consisting of approximately 120 short tons without any further effort to obtain
                    payment for the entire original shipment, and expresses the wish that settlement
                    be made accordingly.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
